     zzyydd — ZyDAS ZD1211/ZD1211B USB IEEE 802.11b/g wireless network driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee eehhccii
           ddeevviiccee uuhhccii
           ddeevviiccee oohhccii
           ddeevviiccee uussbb
           ddeevviiccee zzyydd
           ddeevviiccee wwllaann
           ddeevviiccee wwllaann__aammrrrr

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           if_zyd_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The zzyydd driver provides support for wireless network adapters based
     around the ZyDAS ZD1211 and ZD1211B USB chips.

     zzyydd supports ssttaattiioonn and mmoonniittoorr mode operation.  Only one virtual inter‐
     face may be configured at any time.  For more information on configuring
     this device, see ifconfig(8).

